WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.960
For much of Star Wars visual media, the&nbsp;
focus has been predominantly on people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.520
whose last name is Skywalker. Even with&nbsp;
shows like The Clone Wars animated series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.360
which introduced fans to a young&nbsp;
Padawan by the name of Ahsoka Tano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.240
Anakin's exploits were always front and center.&nbsp;
With The Mandalorian, creators have a chance to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.800
explore a side of the Star Wars universe&nbsp;
that's often gone ignored over the years.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.360
The fate of the galaxy isn't in the balance.&nbsp;
Instead, the plot follows a Mandalorian by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.440
the name of Din Djarin who's tasked with&nbsp;
delivering a child back to its people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.800
As the pair travel to far-off planets, audiences&nbsp;
are introduced to characters and creatures we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.760
never heard of before. For two episodes (so&nbsp;
far) in season 2, audiences have had a chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.520
to spend time with Captain Carson Teva, as played&nbsp;
by Paul Sun-Hyung Lee. Like most actors would be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.720
Lee's ecstatic to be part of this universe.&nbsp;
As he said in an interview with CBC News,

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:58.160
"A Korean-Canadian in the Star Wars universe gives&nbsp;
hope to a lot of people that dreams do come true.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.600
That this is attainable. That's&nbsp;
Star Wars in a nutshell for me."

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.000
Lee had a long journey before landing one of&nbsp;
his biggest roles to date on The Mandalorian.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.720
If you're interested in checking&nbsp;
out the rest of his filmography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.640
then you have a lot of catching up to do.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.240
Paul Sun-Hyung Lee's acting career&nbsp;
stretches back over three decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:20.240
beginning in 1989. Back in the day, he was&nbsp;
credited as simply "Paul Lee" and made numerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:27.040
one-off appearances on a variety of television&nbsp;
programs, such as Total Recall 2070, Soul Food,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:33.760
and Doc. Millennials may recognize the actor as&nbsp;
Bruno Hong Fat in the 1996 film Harriet the Spy.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:39.600
Lee saw his career break out in a big way when&nbsp;
he was cast in the Canadian soap opera Train 48.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:47.440
Lee starred in 256 episodes of the series, which&nbsp;
ran from 2003 to 2005 and followed the lives of 12&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.640
commuters and their interactions on their train&nbsp;
to work. Lee played Randy Ko, a mild-mannered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:57.840
engineer as well as a science-fiction enthusiast.&nbsp;
We learn that he was dumped by his fiancée, but he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:03.440
soon enters another relationship with Liz, another&nbsp;
one of the commuters. However, their relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.800
also ultimately fails when she decides to&nbsp;
conceive a child via artificial insemination.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.800
The show may have ended, but it was just&nbsp;
the start of an extremely prolific career.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.520
Train 48 wouldn't be the last time you could&nbsp;
see Paul Sun-Hyung Lee on Canadian television.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.560
He also made appearances on series like&nbsp;
1-800-MISSING and Billable Hours. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.320
if you were a teenager around 2010,&nbsp;
then chances are good you recognize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.240
him best for his role as Juan Tong&nbsp;
on Degrassi: The Next Generation.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:35.520
While based out of Canada, the series saw immense&nbsp;
success across the border in the United States.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:41.120
Teenagers on the program had to deal with a host&nbsp;
of taboo issues, such as bullying, teen pregnancy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.760
and body image issues. Fortunately, Lee managed&nbsp;
to stay away from those kinds of problems.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:49.840
As Juan Tong, he was the owner of Little&nbsp;
Miss Steaks, which employed some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:55.360
kids at Degrassi High. He appeared in six&nbsp;
episodes spanning across seasons 10 and 11.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.840
After that, Lee starred in TV series like&nbsp;
Almost Heroes and Shoot the Messenger.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.360
He also had a small role&nbsp;
in the 2014 RoboCop reboot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.080
but it was all leading up to a prominent role with&nbsp;
which Netflix subscribers are all too familiar.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.520
Kim's Convenience may have debuted on&nbsp;
Canadian television, but it's become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:16.880
a hit with audiences all over the globe ever&nbsp;
since it hit Netflix. Lee plays Kim Sang-il,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.440
patriarch of the family running a convenience&nbsp;
store in a Toronto neighborhood. He's traditional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.280
when it comes to his Korean roots, which&nbsp;
means he can be stubborn at times but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.840
ultimately just wants what's best for his family.&nbsp;
He has an estranged relationship with his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:35.360
Jung (Shang-Chi star Simu Liu), but they gradually&nbsp;
work on making it better throughout the series.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.000
All four seasons are now available to watch on&nbsp;
Netflix, and fans can look forward to plenty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:46.000
more Kim's Convenience in the years to come. CBC&nbsp;
announced earlier in 2020 that the show was picked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.840
up for two more seasons. No release date&nbsp;
has been announced for the new episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:54.720
which may well be held up by COVID-19&nbsp;
restrictions (via TV Series Finale),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.400
but sooner or later, you'll be&nbsp;
able to see Appa back at it again.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.640
As Captain Carson Teva, Lee's reaching&nbsp;
his biggest audience yet. Hopefully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.320
it won't be the last time he ventures&nbsp;
into major blockbuster properties,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.920
because he brings a natural gravitas&nbsp;
to this larger-than-life universe.

